            </profile>
            <profile id="0f87-f2fa-2d96-f67b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword, javelins and buckler. May have light armour (+3), throwing spears (+4), sling (+3), horse (M7, +8). Army General. Up to two Character Advantages. In a chariot (Chieftain Chariot advantage): M8 WS6 BS6 S4 T4 W3 I6 A4 Ld9. Not available to Scotti Raiders and Settlers. Character Advantages: up to two for an Army General, one for any other character only if the army list allows it. Each advantage may be taken once per 1,000 points (or part thereof) in the army and once per character (not enforced). (The Age of Arthur p.75)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="0c3c-8938-8228-cafc" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">6+ with Buckler +1 in hand-to-hand only</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
