  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2c2d-1e9c-ee77-8467" name="The Scots-Irish (Age of Arthur) - List Notes" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false">
      <description>THE SCOTS-IRISH (The Age of Arthur, pp.71-79). Units of Fianna and Ceithern may have a Leader (+5), Musician (+5) and Standard (+5). Allies are documented only. King's Champion: if the army is led by a Ri Tuath, a single Curadh may be designated King's Champion with up to three Character Advantages (no advantage more than once; points paid as normal); he may never refuse a challenge. Heroes in Chariots: a squadron of at least three characters in chariots deployed at the start of the battle (each chariot counts as two models; no Leader, Standard or Musician; see the book).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Scots-Irish - Scotti Raiders and Settlers]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 20%
  SCOTS-IRISH RAIDERS AND SETTLERS. Characters up to 33% (no Ri Tuath: led by a Curadh upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Fianna and Ceithern). Uncommon up to 20% (Tilgeyr and Irish Wolfhounds). Allies up to 25% from one list: British and Welsh Kingdoms (British Kingdoms or Welsh Kingdoms in the West; Combrogi led by 0-1 Tiern or 0-1 Uchelwyr) or the Picts (Early or Later Southern Pictish Kingdoms or Picts of the North; Pictish Warriors led by Mormaer or Champion). Curadh and Toiseach may not ride in chariots (except a Curadh upgraded to Army General who takes Chieftain Chariot).
[Scots-Irish - Dalriada]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 20%
  DALRIADA. Characters up to 33% (led by a Curadh upgraded to Army General; no Druid). Common warriors at least 33% (Fianna and Ceithern). Uncommon up to 20% (Tilgeyr and Irish Wolfhounds). Allies up to 25% from one list: British and Welsh Kingdoms (British Kingdoms or Welsh Kingdoms in the West) or the Picts (Early or Later Southern Pictish Kingdoms or Picts of the North). Mounted Ceithern may not be fielded; no characters in chariots; a King's Champion may be taken (documented).
[Scots-Irish - Kingdoms of Ireland]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE KINGDOMS OF IRELAND. Characters up to 33% (40% if the army features a squadron of Heroes in Chariots), led by a Ri Tuath or a Curadh upgraded to Army General. Common warriors at least 33% (Fianna and Ceithern). Uncommon up to 25% (Tilgeyr and Irish Wolfhounds). Allies up to 25% from the Scots-Irish - Dalriada (Ceithern led by 0-1 Curadh or 0-1 Toiseach). Any Curadh and Toiseach may ride in chariots. A King's Champion may be taken; characters in chariots may form a chariot squadron (Heroes in Chariots; both documented).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
